---
import SubpageLayout from "../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../utils/url";

const toc = [
  { href: "#who-its-for", label: "Who it's for" },
  { href: "#table-of-contents", label: "Table of contents" },
];

const bookSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Book",
  name: "The Day After AI",
  author: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Enrico Piovesan",
  },
  description: "Making Software Companies Legible to AI Agents.",
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: "Apress",
  },
  isbn: "9798868834516",
  url: new URL(withBase("/about-the-book/"), Astro.site).toString(),
  inLanguage: "en",
  genre: "Software Engineering",
};
---

<SubpageLayout
  title="About the Book"
  description="The Day After AI: Making Software Companies Legible to AI Agents, by Enrico Piovesan. Forthcoming from Apress. ISBN 9798868834516."
  section="book"
  toc={toc}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(bookSchema)} />
  <h1>The Day After AI</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Making Software Companies Legible to AI Agents.
  </p>

  <p>
    Tribal knowledge is the hidden bottleneck preventing every software
    organization from effectively leveraging AI agents. The knowledge
    that lives in people's heads, in Slack threads, in undocumented
    decisions, is not a documentation problem. It is a structural
    problem, and it has a structural solution.
  </p>
  <p>
    <em>The Day After AI</em> gives every role in a software organization a
    concrete recipe for that shift. The organizations that make it first
    will compound that advantage with every agent generation that
    follows. The ones that don't will find themselves outpaced not by
    better technology, but by better structure, the kind their
    competitors built while the window was still open.
  </p>
  <p>
    Forthcoming from Apress. ISBN 9798868834516.
  </p>
  <p>
    Appendix A names the
    <a href="https://enricopiovesan.com/whitepapers/c-dad/">C-DAD white paper</a>
    as the place for the twenty-one principles, the contract lifecycle,
    and the adoption playbook.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-its-for">Who it's for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Architects designing the capability graph and writing the contracts that govern it.</li>
    <li>Developers and tech leads shipping inside and outside a legacy codebase.</li>
    <li>PMs and POs deciding what gets extracted first.</li>
    <li>Designers working in systems that now have to explain themselves to a machine.</li>
    <li>Engineering leaders deciding how much autonomy to hand to AI agents, and how to restructure for it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="table-of-contents">Table of contents</h2>
  <ol class="toc">
    <li id="part-0">
      Part 0: Monday Morning
      <ol>
        <li><a href={withBase("/excerpt/")}>Monday Morning</a></li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li id="introduction">
      <a href={withBase("/introduction/")}>Introduction</a>
    </li>
    <li id="part-i">
      Part I: The Problem
      <ol>
        <li><a href={withBase("/the-day-after/")}>Chapter 1: The Day After</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/tribal-knowledge/")}>Chapter 2: Tribal Knowledge Is the Bottleneck</a></li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li id="part-ii">
      Part II: The Architecture
      <ol>
        <li><a href={withBase("/contracts/")}>Chapter 3: Contracts Are the Answer</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/capabilities-graph/")}>Chapter 4: Capability Graphs, the New Atomic Unit</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/extraction-over-refactoring/")}>Chapter 5: Extraction Over Refactoring</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/making-your-system-legible/")}>Chapter 6: Making Your System Legible to AI Agents</a></li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li id="part-iii">
      Part III: The Transformation
      <ol>
        <li><a href={withBase("/for-architects/")}>Chapter 7: The Architect</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/for-developers/")}>Chapter 8: The Developer</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/for-product-managers/")}>Chapter 9: The PM / PO</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/for-designers/")}>Chapter 10: The Designer</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/for-engineering-leaders/")}>Chapter 11: Leadership</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/company-that-gets-there-first/")}>Chapter 12: The Company That Gets There First</a></li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li id="appendices">
      Appendices
      <ol>
        <li><a href={withBase("/appendix/c-dad-specification/")}>Appendix A: The C-DAD Specification</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/appendix/mcp-documentation-and-implementation-resources/")}>Appendix B: MCP Documentation and Implementation Resources</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/appendix/agent-onboarding-test/")}>Appendix C: The Agent Onboarding Test</a></li>
        <li><a href={withBase("/appendix/interaction-contract-template/")}>Appendix D: The Interaction Contract Template</a></li>
      </ol>
    </li>
  </ol>
</SubpageLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .toc {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .toc ol {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .toc a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border);
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .toc a:hover {
    color: var(--coral);
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }
</style>
